        "original_id": "e5ff3f87-9de0-5658-b4bd-432b0b6e9d7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: 20th Century Fox\n- Works: The Ghost and Mrs. Muir, The Ghost and Mr. Chicken, Good Neighbor Sam, The Shakiest Gun in the West, The Reluctant Astronaut\n- People: Everett Greenbaum, Don Knotts\n- Places: United Kingdom, Century City, Los Angeles, Beverly Hills\n- Concepts: Big Six major American film studios, film rights\n\nFacts:\n- In 1945, 20th Century Fox bought the film rights to the novel The Ghost and Mrs. Muir, which at that time had been published only in the United Kingdom.\n- In 1947, The Ghost and Mrs. Muir was released as a film.\n- 20th Century Fox is one of the Big Six major American film studios.\n- 20th Century Fox is located in the Century City area of Los Angeles, just west of Beverly Hills.\n- The title The Ghost and Mr. Chicken is presumably a humorous variation of the film title The Ghost and Mrs. Muir.\n- Everett Greenbaum wrote the Hollywood feature film Good Neighbor Sam.\n- Everett Greenbaum wrote a series of films starring Don Knotts that included The Shakiest Gun in the West, The Reluctant Astronaut, and The Ghost and Mr. Chicken.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
